diff --git a/news/whats-new.txt b/news/whats-new.txt
index 481adb99..a7e967c1 100644
--- a/news/whats-new.txt
+++ b/news/whats-new.txt
@@ -338,3 +338,4 @@
 2026-11-27 | direction | Harder from planet 2 on: ordinary slime takes about half again as many hits (planet 2 needs 1.75 where it was 1.25, the home world 4.5 where it was 3), raids march with a bigger share of the slime, and mini-bosses come sooner and more often, with the mortar from planet 3 instead of 4. Planet 1 is unchanged | Start a new run and play past the landing world
 2026-11-27 | look | Fewer, shorter messages at the top left: at most three at once instead of five, gone after 4 seconds (6 for red ones such as a lost soldier) instead of 6, and the same message again counts up ("A soldier was killed by the slime ×3") instead of stacking. The long ones are cut to a short phrase ("Ore landed: stand a squad on it for shop points", "A heart is growing on a crystal (Space to look)") | Play any planet and lose a soldier or two
 2026-11-27 | squad | Turrets set to the squads' own loadout fire the plain rifle and two cards again, so they can't copy your squad's gun and cards for free; put a gun in another loadout for them. A gun for sale says which loadout it goes into, a turret's Loadout button names its gun, and the reach ring on a hovered turret matches its own gun. Render still pays within the rifle's reach whatever gun the turret holds | In the shop, show Loadout 2, buy a gun into it and pick Turrets use this
+2026-11-27 | enemy | Planet 7's Grudge readout now shows the share of your hits its scar tissue shrugged off over the last 10 seconds (about half once you have held one spot for 40 seconds), instead of the share of the slime on old scar, which stayed near 1% | Planet 7 of a run: hold one spot and watch the shield readout under the goal
